  "findings": [
    {
      "path": "testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/AssertEvents.java",
      "line": 483,
      "severity": "fix",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "isAccessTokenId matcher has inverted condition and wrong offsets",
      "body": "The line `if (items[0].substring(3, 5).equals(expectedGrantShortcut)) return false;` returns false when the shortcut matches, so a correct token fails the match. The token id is `<st:2><tt:2><gt:2>`, so the grant shortcut is at `substring(4, 6)`, not `(3, 5)`. As written, the matcher rejects `onrtac:uuid` for expected `ac`, and it accepts any id whose chars 3-4 differ from the shortcut. It also throws StringIndexOutOfBounds when the prefix is shorter than 5 chars. Use `if (!items[0].substring(4, 6).equals(expectedGrantShortcut)) return false;` and check the length first.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/protocol/oidc/encode/AccessTokenContext.java",
      "line": 73,
      "severity": "fix",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "Null check for rawTokenId tests grantType instead",
      "body": "`Objects.requireNonNull(grantType, \"Null rawTokenId not allowed\")` checks the wrong argument, so a null rawTokenId passes validation. It would later be encoded as the string \"null\". It should be `Objects.requireNonNull(rawTokenId, ...)`.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "server-spi-private/src/main/java/org/keycloak/protocol/oidc/grants/OAuth2GrantTypeFactory.java",
      "line": 33,
      "severity": "consider",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "title": "New abstract method breaks existing custom grant factories",
      "body": "`getShortcut()` is added as an abstract interface method. Any third-party OAuth2GrantTypeFactory will no longer compile or load (AbstractMethodError). If the intent is to allow extensions, a default method is safer. Also, the factory's postInit calls getShortcut() and puts null into a ConcurrentHashMap, which throws an NPE and aborts startup. Validate for null and for a length of exactly 2, because decoding assumes a fixed 6-char prefix.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "server-spi-private/src/main/java/org/keycloak/protocol/oidc/grants/OAuth2GrantType.java",
      "line": 102,
      "severity": "consider",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "low",
      "title": "grantType is not refreshed when form params are replaced",
      "body": "`grantType` is read once from formParams in the constructor, but `setFormParams` (line 105) can replace the params without updating it. The constructor also NPEs if formParams is null. The copy constructor was removed in the same change. I found no remaining callers of it or of setFormParams in the repo, so I did not confirm a live impact.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    }
  ],
  "contracts": [],
  "summary": "Two clear bugs: the test matcher `isAccessTokenId` in AssertEvents has an inverted condition and wrong substring offsets, and `AccessTokenContext` null-checks the wrong argument for rawTokenId. Two smaller concerns: the new abstract `getShortcut()` breaks custom grant factories, and `Context.grantType` is not refreshed by `setFormParams`. I did not trace how token IDs are consumed after the format change.",
